From 4285fa9538891fd49e1f732a3a646cf49547eabf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Destrudos6 <3411622425@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:52:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Split subtitle style editor into fixed preview plus
 tabbed parameter pages

The style dialog previously scrolled as one piece: scrolling down to a
slider pushed the preview off screen, and the ten-plus controls formed
a single wall of sliders that was hard to scan.

- Keep the preview fixed above the parameters: adjusting any slider
  now always shows its effect live
- Group the parameters into three tabs (text, background, layout), so
  each page holds only a few related controls
- Show the current value (percent, dp, scale) next to every slider
  label and update it while dragging
- Darken the preview backdrop to a cinema-like gradient so translucent
  backgrounds read better
